          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong diffeological space
            is a type of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            but also naturally captures other spaces that one would like to think of as smooth spaces but aren’t manifolds; for example, the space of all smooth maps between two smooth manifolds can be made into a diffeological space. (These mapping spaces are rarely manifolds themselves, see
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds+of+mapping+spaces"} manifolds of mapping spaces
          %p
            In a little more detail, a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong diffeology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            on a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
            of Euclidean spaces with smooth maps as morphisms. To each open set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Set(U,X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Set(U,X)
            are to be regarded as the “smooth functions” from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong diffeological space
            is then a set together with a diffeology on it.
          %p
            Diffeological spaces were originally introduced in (
            %a{:href => "#Souriau79"}> Souriau 79
            ). They have subsequently been developed in the textbook (
            %a{:href => "#PIZ"}> Iglesias-Zemmour 13
            )
          %h2#definition Definition
          #DiffSp.num_defn{:style => "border:solid #cccccc;border-width:2px 1px;padding:0 1em;margin:0 1em;"}
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪𝓅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{Op}
              denote the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              whose objects are the open subsets of the Euclidean spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              and whose morphisms are
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+map"} smooth map
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪𝓅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{Op}
              is generated by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              of open covers, i.e., a family of maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i\to X\}_{i\in I}
              is a covering family if every map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i\to X
              is an open embedding and the union of the images of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              equals
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              A
              %strong diffeological space
              is a pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{D})
              where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is a set
              %li
                %p
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒪𝓅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D} \in Sh(\mathcal{Op})
                  is a
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeology"} diffeology
                  on
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      a
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subsheaf
                      of the sheaf
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mo ↦
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \mapsto Hom_{Set}(U,X)
                      with
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒟
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}(*) = X
                  %li
                    %p
                      equivalently: a
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaf"} concrete sheaf
                      on the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒪𝓅
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{Op}
                      such that
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒟
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}(*) = X
                      \- a
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+object"} concrete
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
                      (see there for more details).
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              of diffeological spaces is a morphism of the corresponding
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi DiffeologicalSp
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DiffeologicalSp \hookrightarrow Sh(CartSp)
              to be the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              on the diffeological spaces in the sheaf topos.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{D})
            a diffeological space, and for any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒪𝓅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in \mathcal{Op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}(U)
            is also called the set of
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            smoothly into the would-be space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em defined
            what it means for a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
            of sets to be smooth.
          %p
            For some comments on the reasoning behind this kind of definition of generalized
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+sheaves%2C+cohomology+and+higher+stacks"} motivation for sheaves, cohomology and higher stacks
          %p
            A sheaf on the site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪𝓅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{Op}
            of open subsets of Euclidean spaces is completely specified by its restriction to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi 𝒪𝓅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp \hookrightarrow \mathcal{Op}
            is a
            = succeed "-inclusion." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subsite"} dense subsite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
          %p
            One may define a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            to be
            %em any
            sheaf of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaf"} concrete sheaf
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+site"} concrete site
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets#DiffeologicalSpacesAreTheConcreteSmoothSets"} this Prop.
            at
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} geometry of physics – smooth sets
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  DiffeologicalSpaces \hookrightarrow Sh(CartSp)
          %p
            on all concrete sheaves is not a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
          %p
            This is Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiffeologicalSpacesAreTheConcreteSmoothSets"}
            below.
          %p
            The concreteness condition on the sheaf is a reiteration of the fact that a diffeological space is a subsheaf of the sheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \mapsto X^{|U|}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as it is determined by the sheaf on the one-point open subset of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^0
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi CartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in CartSp
                to be the ordinary
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi Diff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      X : U \mapsto Hom_{Diff}(U,X)
                      \\,.
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                two diffeological spaces, their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                as sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
                becomes a diffeological space whose
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
                are pairs consisting of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plot"} plot
                into
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and one into
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi DiffSp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi DiffSp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      X \times Y : U \mapsto Hom_{DiffSp}(U,X) \times Hom_{DiffSp}(U,Y)
                      \\,.
            %li
              %p
                Given any two diffeological spaces
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi DiffSp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{DiffSp}(X,Y)
                becomes a smooth space by taking the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
                on some
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                to be the smooth morphisms
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi U
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times U \to Y
                = succeed "-parameterized" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi DiffSp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      [X,Y] : U \mapsto Hom_{DiffSp}(X \times U, Y)
                      \\,.
              %p
                In this formula we regard
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Diff
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in CartSp \hookrightarrow Diff
                as a diffeological space according to the above example. In fact, we apply secretly here the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
                and use the general formula for the cartesian
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on presheaves
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToTopologicalSpaces
            Relation to topological and
            = succeed "-generated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
          %div
            #AdjunctionBetweenTopologicalSpacesAndDiffeologicalSpaces.num_prop
              %h6#proposition Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+between+topological+spaces+and+diffeological+spaces"}> adjunction between topological spaces and diffeological spaces
                  )
              %p
                There is a pair of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              #eq:AdjointFunctorsBetweenTopSpAndDifflgSp.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TopSp
                      %munderover
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi Cdfflg
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mi Dtplg
                      %mi DifflgSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      TopSp
                      \\underoverset{
                      \\underset{
                      Cdfflg
                      }{\longrightarrow}
                      }{
                      \\overset{
                      Dtplg
                      }{\longleftarrow}
                      }{\phantom{AA}\bot\phantom{AA}}
                      DifflgSp
              %p
                between the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} TopologicalSpaces
                and of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DiffeologicalSpaces"} DiffeologicalSpaces
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Cdfflg
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cdfflg
                    takes a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                    to the
                    = succeed "," do
                      %strong continuous diffeology
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_s
                    whose plots
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi s
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_s \to X_s
                    are the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                    (from the underlying
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                    of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
                    = succeed ")." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Dtplg
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dtplg
                    takes a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
                    to the
                    %strong diffeological topology
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topology"}> D-topology
                    ), namely the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                    with the same underlying set
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_s
                    and with the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+topology"} final topology
                    that makes all its plots
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi s
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{s} \to X_{s}
                    into
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                    = succeed "." do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topology"} D-topology
                  %p
                    Hence a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi O
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mo ♭
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O \subset \flat X
                    is an
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                    in the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topology"} D-topology
                    precisely if for each plot
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi U
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon U \to X
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(O) \subset U
                    is an
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                    in the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %p Moreover:
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} fixed points of this adjunction
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ∈
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} TopologicalSpaces
                    (those for which the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
                    is an
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Delta-generated+topological+spaces"} Delta-generated topological spaces
                    (
                    %a{:href => "Delta-generated+topological+space#AsDTopologicalSpaces"} i.e.
                    = succeed "):" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topological+spaces"} D-topological spaces
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mtext is
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi Δ
                          %mtext -generated
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ⇔
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi Dtplg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Cdfflg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %munderover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ≃
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %msub
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mi X
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          X \;\,\text{is}\;\Delta\text{-generated}
                          \\;\;\;\;\;
                          \\Leftrightarrow
                          \\;\;\;\;\;
                          Dtplg(Cdfflg(X))
                          \\underoverset{\simeq}{\;\;\epsilon_X\;\;}{\longrightarrow}
                          X
                %li
                  %p
                    this is an
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
                    = succeed "-generated/" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topological+spaces"} D-topological spaces
                    as a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
                    inside
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
                    and a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
                    inside all
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              #eq:DeltaGeneratedSpacesInIdempotentAdjunction.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TopologicalSpaces
                      %munderover
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi Cdfflg
                        %mover
                          %mo ↩
                          %mrow
                      %mi DTopologicalSpaces
                      %munderover
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                        %munder
                          %mo ↪
                          %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mi Dtplg
                      %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      TopologicalSpaces
                      \\underoverset
                      {
                      \\underset{
                      Cdfflg
                      }{\longrightarrow}
                      }
                      {
                      \\overset{
                      }{\hookleftarrow}
                      }
                      {\phantom{AA}\bot\phantom{AA}}
                      DTopologicalSpaces
                      \\underoverset
                      {
                      \\underset{
                      }{\hookrightarrow}
                      }
                      {
                      \\overset{
                      Dtplg
                      }{\longleftarrow}
                      }
                      {\phantom{AA}\bot\phantom{AA}}
                      DiffeologicalSpaces
              %p
                Finally, these adjunctions are a sequence of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
                with respect to the:
              %table
                %thead
                  %tr
                    %th
                    %th
                    %th
                %tbody
                  %tr
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+D-topological+spaces"} model structure on D-topological spaces
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+diffeological+spaces"} model structure on diffeological spaces
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Caution: There was a gap in the original proof that
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi DTopologicalSpaces
                          %msub
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Quillen
                          %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DTopologicalSpaces \simeq_{Quillen} DiffeologicalSpaces
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "model+structure+on+diffeological+spaces#References"} here
            %p
              Essentially these adjunctions and their properties are observed in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "diffeological+space#SYH10"} Shimakawa, Yoshida &amp; Haraguchi 2010, Prop. 3.1, Prop. 3.2, Lem. 3.3
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "D-topology#CSW13"} Christensen, Sinnamon &amp; Wu 2014, Sec. 3.2
              %a{:href => "#model+structure+on+Delta-generated+topological+spaces#Haraguchi13"} Haraguchi 13, Thm. 3.3
              (on the left) and
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+diffeological+spaces#HaraguchiShimakawa13"} Haraguchi-Shimakawa 13, Sec. 7
              (on the right).
            .proof
              %h6#proof Proof
              %p
                We spell out the existence of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DeltaGeneratedSpacesInIdempotentAdjunction"} (2)
              %p
                First, to see we have an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Dtplg
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi Cdfflg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dtplg \dashv Cdfflg
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#eq:HomIsomorphismForAdjointFunctors"} here
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in DiffeologicalSpaces
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi TopologicalSpaces
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \in TopologicalSpaces
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_s
                for the underlying sets. Then a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      f \;\colon\; Dtplg(X) \longrightarrow Y
                      \\,,
              %p
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi s
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi s
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_s \colon X_s \to Y_s
                of the underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                such that for every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset Y_s
                and every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                of the form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi s
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi s
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_s \circ \phi_s)^{-1}(A) \subset \mathbb{R}^n
                is open. But this means equivalently that for every such
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ \phi
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_s
                constitutes a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo ˜
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Cdfflg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde f \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow Cdfflg(Y)
              %p
                In summary, we thus have a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Dtplg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mi s
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo ˜
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi s
                              %mo =
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Hom( Dtplg(X), Y )
                      \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                      Hom(X, Cdfflg(Y))
                      \\\
                      f_s &amp;\mapsto&amp; (\widetilde f)_s = f_s
                      }
              %p
                given simply as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity
                on the underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                of underlying sets. This makes it immediate that this hom-isomorphism is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                and this establishes the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              %p
                Next, to see that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topological+spaces"} D-topological spaces
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} fixed points
                of this adjunction, we apply the above
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
                on hom-sets to the case
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Ho
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                              %mi Dtplg
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mi Z
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi s
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Ho\Big( Dtplg\big(Cdfflg(Z)\big), Y\Big)
                      \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                      Hom\big(Cdfflg(Z), Cdfflg(Y)\big)
                      \\\
                      (\epsilon_Z)_s &amp;\mapsto&amp; (\mathrm{id})_s
                      }
              %p
                to find that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+the+adjunction"} counit of the adjunction
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mi X
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Dtplg\big(Cdfflg(X)\big)
                      \\overset{\epsilon_X}{\longrightarrow}
                      X
              %p
                is given by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+sets"} underlying sets
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi s
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\epsilon_X)_s = id_{(X_s)}
              %p
                Therefore
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_X
                is an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_s
                with respect to the topology on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                are precisely those with respect to the topology on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Dtplg
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi Cdfflg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dtplg\big(Cdfflg(X)\big)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                coincide with those whose pre-images under all continuous functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
                are open. This means equivalently that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a D-topological space.
              %p
                Finally, to see that we have an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "idempotent+adjunction#EquivalentConditionsForIdempotency"} this Prop.
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi TopologicalSpaces
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi TopologicalSpaces
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Dtplg \circ Cdfflg
                      \\;\colon\;
                      TopologicalSpaces \longrightarrow TopologicalSpaces
              %p
                is an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+comonad"} idempotent comonad
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi Dtplg
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi η
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi Cdfflg
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Dtplg \circ Cdfflg
                      \\overset{
                      Dtplg \cdot \eta \cdot Cdfflg
                      }{\longrightarrow}
                      Dtplg \circ Cdfflg \circ Dtplg \circ Cdfflg
              %p
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϵ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
                on the underlying sets. Therefore, this being a natural isomorphism is equivalent to the operation of passing to the D-topological refinement of the topology of a topological space being an idempotent operation, which is clearly the case.
          %p
            Further discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topology"} D-topology
            is in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CSW13"} CSW 13
          %h3#OnTopologicalHomotopyTypeAndDiffeologicalShape Topological homotopy type and diffeological shape
          %div
            #DiffeologicalSingularSimplicialSet.num_defn
              %h6#definition Definition
              %p
                %strong (diffeological singular simplicial set)
              %p
                Consider the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Δ
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi Δ
                                    %mi diff
                                    %mo •
                            %mtd
                              %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mi Δ
                                %mi diff
                                %mi n
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ≔
                                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                                  %mover
                                    %mi x
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %msup
                                    %mi ℝ
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi n
                                      %mo +
                                      %mn 1
                                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                  %munder
                                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                                    %mi i
                                  %msup
                                    %mi x
                                    %mi i
                                  %mo =
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\Delta
                      \&amp;
                      \\overset{
                      \\Delta^\bullet_{diff}
                      }{
                      \\longrightarrow
                      }
                      \&amp;
                      DiffeologicalSpaces
                      \\\
                      [n]
                      \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                      \\Delta^n_{diff}
                      \\mathrlap{
                      \\coloneqq
                      \\big\{
                      \\vec x \in \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
                      \\;\vert\;
                      \\underset{i}{\sum} x^i = 1
                      \\big\}
                      }
                      }
              %p
                which in degree
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                is the standard extended
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-simplex"} n-simplex
                inside
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeology"} diffeology
              %p
                This induces a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve and realization
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
                between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
                and
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              #eq:NerveAndRealizationForDiffeologicalSpaces.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
