                    %mi Sing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sing_{diff} \circ Cdfflg
                    \\;
                    \\underoverset
                    {\in \mathrm{W}_{wh}}
                    {}
                    {\longrightarrow}
                    \\;
                    Sing
            %p
              applied to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:AComparisonMoprphismForShapeOfDiffeologicalMappingSpace"} (4)
          %h3#EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoDiffeoloticalSpaces Embedding of smooth manifolds into diffeological spaces
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The obvious functor from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothManifolds"} SmoothManifolds
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DiffeologicalSpaces"} DiffeologicalSpaces
              of diffeological spaces is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothManifolds
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi DiffeologicalSpacess
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SmoothManifolds \hookrightarrow  DiffeologicalSpacess
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is a direct consequence of the fact that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo
                      %mi smooth
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} _{smooth}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+sub-site"} dense sub-site
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothManifolds"} SmoothManifolds
              and the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            %p It may nevertheless be useful to spell out the elementary proof directly:
            %p
              To see that the functor is faithful, notice that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g : X \to Y
              are two
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              of that point. This
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plot"} plot
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plot"} plot
            %p
              To see that the functor is full, we need to show that a map of sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              that sends
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
              is necessarily a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma : (0,1) \to X
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boman%27s+theorem"} Boman's theorem
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              must be smooth.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The proof shows that we could restrict attention to the full sub-site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mrow
                        %mi dim
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp_{dim \leq 1} \subset CartSp
              on the objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^0
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^1
              and still have a full and faithful embedding
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mrow
                        %mi dim
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Diff \hookrightarrow Sh(CartSp_{dim \leq 1})
                    \\,.
            %p
              This fact plays a role in the definition of
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%B6licher+space"} Frölicher space
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
              by curves into and out of them.
            %p
              While the site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mrow
                        %mi dim
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp_{dim \leq 1}
              is more convenient for some purposes, it is not so useful for other purposes, mostly when diffeological spaces are regarded from the point of view of the full sheaf topos: the sheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mrow
                        %mi dim
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(CartSp_{dim \leq 1})
              lacks some non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaf"} concrete
              sheaves of interest, such as the sheaves of differential forms of degree
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq 2
          %h3#embedding_of_smooth_manifolds_with_boundary_into_diffeological_spaces Embedding of smooth manifolds with boundary into diffeological spaces
          #SmoothManifoldsWithBoundaryEmbedIntoDiffeologicalSpaces.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds+with+boundaries+and+corners"} manifolds with boundaries and corners
                form
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            %p
              The evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmthMfdWBdrCrn
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AAAA
                    %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SmthMfdWBdrCrn \overset{\phantom{AAAA}}{\hookrightarrow} DiffeologicalSpaces
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds+with+boundaries+and+corners"} manifolds with boundaries and corners
              to that of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
              = succeed "-embedding." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#PIZ"}> Iglesias-Zemmour 13, 4.16
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GurerIZ19"} Gürer &amp; Iglesias-Zemmour 19
          %h3#EmbeddingOfBanachManifoldsIntoDiffeologicalSpaces Embedding of Banach manifolds into diffeological spaces
          %p
            Also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+manifolds"} Banach manifolds
            embed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} fully faithfully
            into the category of diffeological spaces. In (
            %a{:href => "#Hain"}> Hain
            ) this is discussed in terms of Chen smooth spaces.
          %h3#RelationBetweenDeffeologicalAndFrechetStructure Embedding of Fréchet manifolds into diffeological spaces
          %p
            We discuss a natural embedding of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+manifolds"} Fréchet manifolds
            into the category of diffeological spaces.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Define a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi FrechetManifolds
                    %mo →
                    %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\iota \colon FrechetManifolds \to DiffeologicalSpaces
            %p
              in the evident way by taking for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+manifold"} Fréchet manifold
              for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              the set of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota(X)
              to be the set of smooth functions
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
          #FrechetEmbedding.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi FrechetManifolds
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota \colon FrechetManifolds \hookrightarrow DiffeologicalSpaces
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Losik94"}> Losik 94, theorem 3.1.1
            , following
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Losik92"} Losik 92
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+manifolds"} Banach manifolds
            in (
            %a{:href => "#Hain"}> Hain
            ). The fact that maps between Fréchet spaces are smooth if and only if they send smooth curves to smooth curves was proved earlier in (
            %a{:href => "#Frolicher"}> Frölicher 81, théorème 1
            )
          %p
            The statement is also implied by (
            %a{:href => "#KrieglMichor"}> Kriegl-Michor 97, cor. 3.14
            ) which states that functions between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+convex+vector+spaces"} locally convex vector spaces
            are diffeologically smooth precisely if they send smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curves"} curves
            to smooth curves. This is not true if one uses
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michal-Bastiani+smooth+map"} Michal-Bastiani smoothness
            (
            %a{:href => "#Glockner06"}> Glöckner 06
            ), in which case one merely has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi lctvs
                    %mo →
                    %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lctvs \to DiffeologicalSpaces
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#KrieglMichor"} Kriegl-Michor 97
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SmoothManifold
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in SmoothManifold
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+manifold"} compact manifold
            %p
              Then under this embedding, the diffeological mapping space structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X,Y)_{diff}
              on the mapping space coincides with the Fréchet manifold structure
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Fr
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X,Y)_{Fr}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Fr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi diff
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\iota(C^\infty(X,Y)_{Fr})
                    \\simeq
                    C^\infty(X,Y)_{diff}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Waldorf09"}> Waldorf 09, lemma A.1.7
            ).
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h3#EmbeddingOfDiffeologicalSpacesIntoTheSheafTopos Embedding of diffeological spaces into smooth sets
          %p
            We discuss how diffeological spaces are equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+objects"} concrete objects
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "smooth+set#Cohesion"} there
          #DiffeologicalSpacesAreTheConcreteSmoothSets.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (diffeological spaces are the concrete smooth sets)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+objects"} concrete objects
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothSet
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cart
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothSet \coloneqq Sh(Cart)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the category of diffeological spaces
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaves"} concrete sheaves
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(CartSp)
              are by definition those objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              for which the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi CoDisc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma \dashv CoDisc)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi CoDisc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to CoDisc \Gamma X
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in CartSp
              we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Codisc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X(U) \simeq Hom_{Sh}(U,X) \to Hom_{Sh}(U, Codisc \Gamma X)
                    \\simeq Hom_{Set}(\Gamma U, \Gamma X)
            %p is a monomorphism. This is precisely the condition on a sheaf to be a diffeological space.
          %p
            For a fully detailed proof see
            %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets#DiffeologicalSpacesAreTheConcreteSmoothSets"} this Prop.
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} geometry of physics – smooth sets
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The category of diffeological spaces is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              This follows from the discussion at
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Locality"} Locality
          %p This has some immediate general abstract consequences
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
            %p The category of diffeological spaces is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
          %h3#EmbeddingOfDiffeologicalSpacesIntoHigherDifferentialGeometry Embedding of diffeological spaces into higher differential geometry
          %p
            In the last section we saw the embedding of diffeological spaces as precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+objects"} concrete objects
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SmthMfd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(CartSp) \simeq Sh(SmthMfd)
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sh(CartSp) \hookrightarrow
                  Smooth \infty Grpd \coloneqq Sh_\infty(CartSp)
          %p
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            of “higher
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            – as precisely the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} 0-truncated objects
          %h3#distribution_theory Distribution theory
          %p
            Since a space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            is canonically a diffeological space, it is natural to consider the
            %em smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functionals"} linear functionals
            on such
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+linear+functionals"} continuous linear functionals
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributional+densities"} distributional densities
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions+are+the+smooth+linear+functionals"} distributions are the smooth linear functionals
            for details.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+diffeological+spaces"} model structure on diffeological spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} smooth set
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+vector+space"} diffeological vector space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+groupoid"}> diffeological groupoid
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} diffeological ∞-groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connectology"} connectology
          %h2#References References
          %h3#Introductions Introductions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Iglesias-Zemmour"}> Patrick Iglesias-Zemmour
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Diffeologies
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/New+Spaces+for+Mathematics+and+Physics"} New Spaces for Mathematics and Physics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4sZDmiVOhaA"} video
            %li#IglesiasZemmour18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Iglesias-Zemmour"}> Patrick Iglesias-Zemmour
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An introduction to diffeology
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.turkmath.org/beta/konferans.php?id_konferans=365"} Modern Mathematics Methods in Physics: Diffeology, Categories and Toposes and Non-commutative Geometry Summer School
                (2018)
              %p
                published in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/New+Spaces+for+Mathematics+and+Physics"} New Spaces for Mathematics and Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781108854429.003"} doi:10.1017/9781108854429.003
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.huji.ac.il/~piz/documents/AITD.pdf"} pdf
            %li#IZ25
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Iglesias-Zemmour"}> Patrick Iglesias-Zemmour
                \:
                %em Why Diffeology?
                (2025) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://math.huji.ac.il/~piz/documents/WD.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesGeneral Foundations
          %p
            The basic idea of understanding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+spaces"} generalized smooth spaces
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaves"} concrete sheaves
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of smooth test spaces originates in work of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuo+Tsai+Chen"} Kuo Tsai Chen
            (see also at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chen+space"} Chen space
          %ul
            %li#Chen73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuo+Tsai+Chen"}> Kuo Tsai Chen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Iterated integrals of differential forms and loop space homology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1970846"} jstor:1970846
          %p
            Chen considered (apart from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+integrals"} iterated integrals
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            on a site of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+subsets"} convex subsets
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
          %ul
            %li#Chen75
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuo+Tsai+Chen"}> Kuo Tsai Chen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Iterated integrals, fundamental groups and covering spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1997148"} jstor:1997148
          %p
            roughly the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            condition was added (without using any of this sheaf-theoretic terminology). The definition of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chen+spaces"} Chen spaces
            stabilized in
          %ul
            %li#Chen77
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuo+Tsai+Chen"}> Kuo Tsai Chen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Iterated path integrals
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.bams/1183539443"} euclid:1183539443
          %p
            and served as the basis of a celebrated theorem on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+spaces"} loop spaces
          %p A brief review is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuo-Tsai+Chen"}> Kuo-Tsai Chen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On differentiable spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"} William Lawvere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Schanuel"} Stephen Schanuel
              (eds.),
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+in+Continuum+Physics"} Categories in Continuum Physics
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0076928"} doi:10.1007/BFb0076928
          %p (which, curiously, still does not make the connection to the theory of sheaves).
          %p#However
            However, Chen does not require the domains of his plots to be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Stacey11"} Stacey 11, p. 32
          %p
            The proper concept of diffeological spaces was introduced, under the name
            %em difféologie
            and apparently independently from Chen, in:
          %ul
            %li#Souriau79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marie+Souriau"}> Jean-Marie Souriau
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Groupes différentiels
                %em Differential Geometrical Methods in Mathematical Physics
                (Proc. Conf., Aix-en-Provence/Salamanca, 1979), Lecture Notes in Math. 836, Springer, Berlin, (1980), pp. 91–128. (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0089728"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0089728
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=607688"} mr:607688
            %li#Souriau84
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marie+Souriau"}> Jean-Marie Souriau
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Groupes différentiels et physique mathématique
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0016198"} doi:10.1007/BFb0016198
          %p
            motivated there by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+groups"} diffeological groups
            arising in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
          %p The article
          %ul
            %li#BaezHoffnung11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Hoffnung"} Alexander Hoffnung
              = succeed "," do
                %em Convenient Categories of Smooth Spaces
              %strong 363
              11 (2011) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0807.1704"}> arXiv:0807.1704
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/41307457"} jstor:41307457
          %p
            proved that diffeological spaces are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaves"} concrete sheaves
            forming a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-topos"} quasi-topos
          %p A discussion of the relations of variants of the definition is in
          %ul
            %li#Stacey11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Stacey"}> Andrew Stacey
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Comparative Smootheology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/25/4/25-04abs.html"} tac:25-04
          %h3#differential_geometry_of_diffeological_spaces Differential geometry of diffeological spaces
          %p
            Following Souriau, a comprehensive textbook account of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            formulated in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            (and coining that term) is
          %ul
            %li#PIZ
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Iglesias-Zemmour"}> Patrick Iglesias-Zemmour
              \:
              %em Diffeology
              Mathematical Surveys and Monographs, AMS (2013) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://math.huji.ac.il/~piz/Site/The%20Book.html"}> web
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-185"} ISBN:978-0-8218-9131-5
          %p following the thesis
          %ul
            %li#IglesiasZemmour85
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Iglesias-Zemmour"}> Patrick Iglesias-Zemmour
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fibrations difféologiques et Homotopie
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://math.huji.ac.il/~piz/Site/The%20Articles/D9DD15EE-6993-4CA3-8B9B-4FC1DEF4A418.html"} web
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://math.huji.ac.il/~piz/documents/TheseEtatPI.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/IglesiasZemmourFibrationsDiffeologiques1985.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p which contains some useful material that may not yet have made it into the book.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+calculus"} Cartan calculus
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            is developed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Blohmann"}> Christian Blohmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Elastic diffeological spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.02583"} arXiv:2301.02583
          %p
            Application to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+connections"} universal connections
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Mostow"}> Mark Mostow
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The differentiable space structures of Milnor classifying spaces, simplicial complexes, and geometric realizations
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214434974"} euclid:jdg/1214434974
          %p More pointers and monthly seminars at:
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://diffeology.net/"} diffeology.net
          %h3#full_subcategories Full subcategories
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-inclusion" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+manifolds"} Banach manifolds
            into the category of diffeological spaces is due to
          %ul
            %li#Hain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Hain"}> Richard Hain
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A characterization of smooth functions defined on a Banach space
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/proc/1979-077-01/S0002-9939-1979-0539632-8/home.html"} web
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/proc/1979-077-01/S0002-9939-1979-0539632-8/S0002-9939-1979-0539632-8.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The (non-full) embedding of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+convex+vector+spaces"} locally convex vector spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michal-Bastiani+smooth+maps"} Michal-Bastiani smooth maps
            into diffeological spaces is discussed around corollary 3.14 in
          %ul
            %li#KrieglMichor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Kriegl"}> Andreas Kriegl
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Michor"} Peter Michor
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+convenient+setting+of+global+analysis"} The convenient setting of global analysis
          %p That there are diffeologically-smooth maps between locally convex vector spaces that are not continuous, and a fortiori not smooth in the sense of Michal-Bastiani is given, for instance, in
          %ul
            %li#Glockner06
              Helge Glöckner,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Discontinuous non-linear mappings on locally convex direct limits
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0503387"} arXiv:math/0503387
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-inclusion" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+manifolds"} Fréchet manifolds
            into diffeological spaces is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Losik92
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Losik"}> Mark Losik
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fréchet manifolds as diffeologic spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://dmitripavlov.org/scans/losik-frechet-manifolds-as-diffeologic-spaces.pdf"} PDF
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://mi.mathnet.ru/eng/ivm4812"} mathnet:ivm4812
          %p and reviewed in
          %ul
            %li#Losik94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Losik"}> Mark Losik
              , Section 3 of:
              = succeed "." do
                %em Categorical Differential Geometry
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/CTGDC_1994__35_4_274_0"} numdam:CTGDC_1994__35_4_274_0
          %p The proof can in fact be deduced from théorème 1 of
          %ul
            %li#Frolicher
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alfred+Fr%C3%B6licher"}> Alfred Frölicher
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Applications lisses entre espaces et variétés de Fréchet
              %strong 293
              (1981), no. 2, 125–127.
              %a{:href => "http://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k5533894s/f31.image"} BnF
          %p
            The preservation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            under this embedding is due to
          %ul
            %li#Waldorf09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"}> Konrad Waldorf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Transgression to Loop Spaces and its Inverse I
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.3212"} arXiv:0911.3212
          %p
            The largest
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
            on the set which underlies a diffeological space with respect to which all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plots"} plots
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            (the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topology"}> D-topology
            ”) is studied in
          %ul
            %li#SYH10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuhisa+Shimakawa"}> Kazuhisa Shimakawa
                , K. Yoshida,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadayuki+Haraguchi"} Tadayuki Haraguchi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homology and cohomology via enriched bifunctors
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1010.3336"} arXiv:1010.3336
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2206/kyushujm.72.239"} doi:10.2206/kyushujm.72.239
            %li#CSW13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+Daniel+Christensen"}> J. Daniel Christensen
                , Gord Sinnamon,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enxin+Wu"} Enxin Wu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The
                    = succeed "-topology" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1302.2935"} arXiv:1302.2935
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://msp.org/pjm/2014/272-1/p04.xhtml"} doi:10.2140/pjm.2014.272.87
          %p
            Some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            modeled on diffeological spaces (instead of on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#ChristensenWu13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+Daniel+Christensen"}> J. Daniel Christensen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enxin+Wu"} Enxin Wu
              = succeed "," do
                %em The homotopy theory of diffeological spaces, I. Fibrant and cofibrant objects
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.6394"} arXiv:1311.6394
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-inclusion" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds+with+boundaries+and+corners"} manifolds with boundaries and corners
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#GurerIZ19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serap+G%C3%BCrer"}> Serap Gürer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Iglesias-Zemmour"} Patrick Iglesias-Zemmour
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential forms on manifolds with boundary and corners
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indag.2019.07.004"} doi:10.1016/j.indag.2019.07.004
          %h3#ReferencesForOrbifolds For orbifolds
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            regarded as naive local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+spaces"} quotient spaces
            (instead of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotients"} homotopy quotients
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"} differentiable stacks
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
          %ul
            %li#IKZ10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Iglesias-Zemmour"}> Patrick Iglesias-Zemmour
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yael+Karshon"} Yael Karshon
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Orbifolds as diffeologies
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0501093"} arXiv:math/0501093
            %li#Watts15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jordan+Watts"}> Jordan Watts
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Differential Structure of an Orbifold
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1503.01740"} arXiv:1503.01740
          %p
            On this approach seen in the broader context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Proper+Orbifold+Cohomology"} Proper Orbifold Cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.01101"}> arXiv:2008.01101
              )
        .revisedby
          %p
            Last revised on October 31, 2025 at 08:07:11.
            See the
            %a{:href => "/nlab/history/diffeological+space", :style => "color: #005c19"} history
            of this page for a list of all contributions to it.
